cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-memory-meter: measuring the real memory footprint of a local LLM from its official configuration"
abstract: >-
  Companion program for the article "Como saber se um modelo de IA roda no seu computador
  — e por quê" (Carlos Ulisses Flores, 2026). The one-line KV-cache formula that
  circulates widely (batch x context x layers x hidden_size x 2 x bytes) is exact only for
  pure Multi-Head Attention, and overestimates a 2026 hybrid model by up to 20x. This
  zero-dependency program reads a model's official config.json and reports both figures
  side by side, applying Grouped-Query Attention, sliding-window saturation, constant-size
  linear/recurrent state, shared K=V, and real quantization bit-widths. Measured on
  Qwen3.8-27B (19.8x overestimate at 256K context) and Gemma 4 26B A4B (8.2x). Every
  number the article publishes is asserted by the test suite against frozen upstream
  configs and sealed in a SHA-256 provenance chain.
